using data aws_iam_policy_document instead of jsonencode for multiple Statement
using for each for multiple modules creating instead of harcoding them
using a boolean is_service_name on api's modules creation(worker-service do not have a port, it's just sns/sqs fan out)
ls_framework_core been doing too much()
circular dependency
treating my workerservice like a web service, it’s just an ECS Fargate task consuming SQS/SNS events.
dynamically creating both my api services and workerservice under the same module by using is_service_name 
no need to provide from_port and to_port for aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule
rds db beeing recreated on each terraform apply
You’re running into a classic Terraform “cascade replacement” problem caused by one small attribute change breaking computed dependencies across multiple resources.(move front end s3 policy to a single place into cloudfront policy)
created multiple ci/cd pipelines for internal services, gateway-api service, frontend.. Best practice create only one ci/cd pipeline
no connection was established between codepipeline and my github
A common improvement is to add path filtering. and only trigger the relevant pipeline. avoiding many unnecessary builds.
one nat gateway for each subnets
circular dependencies

